@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# The start menu's sound line (UI & UX, 2026-11-07; the EP's brief from Audio's docs/audio/pad-start.md; parked behind the host's hook)
+
+**What and why.** A browser keeps a page's sound suspended until the page has had a key, a click or a touch. Audio now asks the browser to start the sound on a pad press too, but whether a real pad press counts is only known from Orb's next play file (the audio status line's `pad seen N asked N woke N`). If a pad does not count, a player who starts with the pad alone hears nothing, and nothing on screen says why. This line says it once, on the start menu, and only while the browser is holding the sound.
+
+**The line.** `prompt.menu_sound_blocked`: "Sound starts when you press a key or click" (ui/data/terms.json; Narrative may reword it). One small line in the start menu's small type, last, under Reduce flashing's line at the bottom of the card, in the same dim ink. No icon, no colour, nothing animated.
+
+**When it shows.** Only on the start menu card (the first screen of a session), never the pause-time menu, and only while the host's hook says the sound is blocked:
+- `UiHud.web_blocked_fn` is a callable `() -> bool`. It is read once a frame while the start menu is up. Unset (every desktop build, every tool, the demo) means no line.
+- The host's one line (a grant, `render/core/main.gd`): `ui_hud.web_blocked_fn = func() -> bool: return audio != null and audio.web_blocked()`. Audio's `web_blocked()` is read only and asks the page at most twice a second; false off the web.
+- When a key or click wakes the sound the answer turns false, and the line goes in the same frame as a clean cut (the card's redraw key carries the flag). Nothing fades.
+
+**Where it can never be.** It is part of the card at the screen's edge: never over, on or between the fighters (the menu holds the match). On a card too short for it (a small phone sideways, a large Text size) the line is the first thing dropped, before the card's own note and before anything the card needs; it never makes the card stop fitting.
+
+**Not built here.** The pad press's own handling and the shell snippet are Audio's and Tools'. The line is a courtesy: if Orb's next play shows a pad wakes the sound (`woke` above 0 after a pad press), this park need not land.
+
+**Tests (`_sound_line_rules`, 5 checks in hud_check):** the words; the flag on adds one last line at desktop, short and upright sizes and with it off nothing changes; where the card is too tall the line goes and the card still fits; the pause-time menu never shows it; in the HUD an unset hook shows nothing, true adds the line and changes the redraw key, false takes it away. Each of the two halves fails without its code (tried).
+
+**Demo:** `--menu --sound` (the demo's start menu with the hook answering true).
